        "pt-BR": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needsReview",
            "value": "Usage:\n  cmux vm layout export <machine> [<workspace-id|name>] [--raw]\n                                                      Print a machine workspace's layout as a declarative layout\n                                                      document — the same JSON `cmux new-workspace --layout`,\n                                                      `cmux layout save/open`, and cmux.json use. Default: the\n                                                      machine's focused workspace. --raw prints the daemon's own\n                                                      LayoutDocument (exact pane/tab ids) instead.\n  cmux vm layout apply <machine> (<file>|- | --from-saved <name>) [--workspace <workspace-id>|--name <name>] [--cwd <dir>] [--open]\n                                                      Build panes, splits, and tabs on the machine from a layout\n                                                      document: a file, stdin (-), or a layout saved on this Mac\n                                                      (`cmux layout list`). Default: a NEW machine workspace named\n                                                      after the document (--name overrides); --workspace targets an\n                                                      existing EMPTY workspace. Terminal `command`s are typed into\n                                                      login shells started in each surface's `cwd` (relative to\n                                                      --cwd, default: the work user's home). --open then opens the workspace here\n                                                      with the same geometry.\n\nDocument (one of):\n  {\"pane\": {\"surfaces\": [{\"type\": \"terminal\", \"name\": \"tests\", \"command\": \"bun test\", \"cwd\": \"work/app\"}]}}\n  {\"direction\": \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\", \"split\": 0.6, \"children\": [<node>, <node>]}\n  {\"name\": …, \"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}      or      {\"name\": …, \"workspace\": {\"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}}\n`horizontal` = side by side (first child left), `vertical` = stacked (first child top); `split` is the\nfirst child's share (0.1–0.9, default 0.5). Surface types: terminal (name, command, cwd, env),\nbrowser (url, name); project surfaces are Mac-only and skipped on a machine.\nWorkspace ids come from `cmux vm tree`. Add --json for the raw result. Exit 2 = the document is invalid."
          }
        },
        "ru": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needsReview",
            "value": "Usage:\n  cmux vm layout export <machine> [<workspace-id|name>] [--raw]\n                                                      Print a machine workspace's layout as a declarative layout\n                                                      document — the same JSON `cmux new-workspace --layout`,\n                                                      `cmux layout save/open`, and cmux.json use. Default: the\n                                                      machine's focused workspace. --raw prints the daemon's own\n                                                      LayoutDocument (exact pane/tab ids) instead.\n  cmux vm layout apply <machine> (<file>|- | --from-saved <name>) [--workspace <workspace-id>|--name <name>] [--cwd <dir>] [--open]\n                                                      Build panes, splits, and tabs on the machine from a layout\n                                                      document: a file, stdin (-), or a layout saved on this Mac\n                                                      (`cmux layout list`). Default: a NEW machine workspace named\n                                                      after the document (--name overrides); --workspace targets an\n                                                      existing EMPTY workspace. Terminal `command`s are typed into\n                                                      login shells started in each surface's `cwd` (relative to\n                                                      --cwd, default: the work user's home). --open then opens the workspace here\n                                                      with the same geometry.\n\nDocument (one of):\n  {\"pane\": {\"surfaces\": [{\"type\": \"terminal\", \"name\": \"tests\", \"command\": \"bun test\", \"cwd\": \"work/app\"}]}}\n  {\"direction\": \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\", \"split\": 0.6, \"children\": [<node>, <node>]}\n  {\"name\": …, \"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}      or      {\"name\": …, \"workspace\": {\"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}}\n`horizontal` = side by side (first child left), `vertical` = stacked (first child top); `split` is the\nfirst child's share (0.1–0.9, default 0.5). Surface types: terminal (name, command, cwd, env),\nbrowser (url, name); project surfaces are Mac-only and skipped on a machine.\nWorkspace ids come from `cmux vm tree`. Add --json for the raw result. Exit 2 = the document is invalid."
          }
        },
        "th": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needsReview",
            "value": "Usage:\n  cmux vm layout export <machine> [<workspace-id|name>] [--raw]\n                                                      Print a machine workspace's layout as a declarative layout\n                                                      document — the same JSON `cmux new-workspace --layout`,\n                                                      `cmux layout save/open`, and cmux.json use. Default: the\n                                                      machine's focused workspace. --raw prints the daemon's own\n                                                      LayoutDocument (exact pane/tab ids) instead.\n  cmux vm layout apply <machine> (<file>|- | --from-saved <name>) [--workspace <workspace-id>|--name <name>] [--cwd <dir>] [--open]\n                                                      Build panes, splits, and tabs on the machine from a layout\n                                                      document: a file, stdin (-), or a layout saved on this Mac\n                                                      (`cmux layout list`). Default: a NEW machine workspace named\n                                                      after the document (--name overrides); --workspace targets an\n                                                      existing EMPTY workspace. Terminal `command`s are typed into\n                                                      login shells started in each surface's `cwd` (relative to\n                                                      --cwd, default: the work user's home). --open then opens the workspace here\n                                                      with the same geometry.\n\nDocument (one of):\n  {\"pane\": {\"surfaces\": [{\"type\": \"terminal\", \"name\": \"tests\", \"command\": \"bun test\", \"cwd\": \"work/app\"}]}}\n  {\"direction\": \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\", \"split\": 0.6, \"children\": [<node>, <node>]}\n  {\"name\": …, \"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}      or      {\"name\": …, \"workspace\": {\"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}}\n`horizontal` = side by side (first child left), `vertical` = stacked (first child top); `split` is the\nfirst child's share (0.1–0.9, default 0.5). Surface types: terminal (name, command, cwd, env),\nbrowser (url, name); project surfaces are Mac-only and skipped on a machine.\nWorkspace ids come from `cmux vm tree`. Add --json for the raw result. Exit 2 = the document is invalid."
          }
        },
        "tr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needsReview",
            "value": "Usage:\n  cmux vm layout export <machine> [<workspace-id|name>] [--raw]\n                                                      Print a machine workspace's layout as a declarative layout\n                                                      document — the same JSON `cmux new-workspace --layout`,\n                                                      `cmux layout save/open`, and cmux.json use. Default: the\n                                                      machine's focused workspace. --raw prints the daemon's own\n                                                      LayoutDocument (exact pane/tab ids) instead.\n  cmux vm layout apply <machine> (<file>|- | --from-saved <name>) [--workspace <workspace-id>|--name <name>] [--cwd <dir>] [--open]\n                                                      Build panes, splits, and tabs on the machine from a layout\n                                                      document: a file, stdin (-), or a layout saved on this Mac\n                                                      (`cmux layout list`). Default: a NEW machine workspace named\n                                                      after the document (--name overrides); --workspace targets an\n                                                      existing EMPTY workspace. Terminal `command`s are typed into\n                                                      login shells started in each surface's `cwd` (relative to\n                                                      --cwd, default: the work user's home). --open then opens the workspace here\n                                                      with the same geometry.\n\nDocument (one of):\n  {\"pane\": {\"surfaces\": [{\"type\": \"terminal\", \"name\": \"tests\", \"command\": \"bun test\", \"cwd\": \"work/app\"}]}}\n  {\"direction\": \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\", \"split\": 0.6, \"children\": [<node>, <node>]}\n  {\"name\": …, \"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}      or      {\"name\": …, \"workspace\": {\"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}}\n`horizontal` = side by side (first child left), `vertical` = stacked (first child top); `split` is the\nfirst child's share (0.1–0.9, default 0.5). Surface types: terminal (name, command, cwd, env),\nbrowser (url, name); project surfaces are Mac-only and skipped on a machine.\nWorkspace ids come from `cmux vm tree`. Add --json for the raw result. Exit 2 = the document is invalid."
          }
        },
        "uk": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "needsReview",
            "value": "Usage:\n  cmux vm layout export <machine> [<workspace-id|name>] [--raw]\n                                                      Print a machine workspace's layout as a declarative layout\n                                                      document — the same JSON `cmux new-workspace --layout`,\n                                                      `cmux layout save/open`, and cmux.json use. Default: the\n                                                      machine's focused workspace. --raw prints the daemon's own\n                                                      LayoutDocument (exact pane/tab ids) instead.\n  cmux vm layout apply <machine> (<file>|- | --from-saved <name>) [--workspace <workspace-id>|--name <name>] [--cwd <dir>] [--open]\n                                                      Build panes, splits, and tabs on the machine from a layout\n                                                      document: a file, stdin (-), or a layout saved on this Mac\n                                                      (`cmux layout list`). Default: a NEW machine workspace named\n                                                      after the document (--name overrides); --workspace targets an\n                                                      existing EMPTY workspace. Terminal `command`s are typed into\n                                                      login shells started in each surface's `cwd` (relative to\n                                                      --cwd, default: the work user's home). --open then opens the workspace here\n                                                      with the same geometry.\n\nDocument (one of):\n  {\"pane\": {\"surfaces\": [{\"type\": \"terminal\", \"name\": \"tests\", \"command\": \"bun test\", \"cwd\": \"work/app\"}]}}\n  {\"direction\": \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\", \"split\": 0.6, \"children\": [<node>, <node>]}\n  {\"name\": …, \"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}      or      {\"name\": …, \"workspace\": {\"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}}\n`horizontal` = side by side (first child left), `vertical` = stacked (first child top); `split` is the\nfirst child's share (0.1–0.9, default 0.5). Surface types: terminal (name, command, cwd, env),\nbrowser (url, name); project surfaces are Mac-only and skipped on a machine.\nWorkspace ids come from `cmux vm tree`. Add --json for the raw result. Exit 2 = the document is invalid."
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "用法：\n  cmux vm layout export <machine> [<workspace-id|name>] [--raw]\n                                                      将机器工作区的布局打印为声明式布局\n                                                      文档 —— 即 `cmux new-workspace --layout`、\n                                                      `cmux layout save/open` 以及 cmux.json 所使用的相同 JSON。默认值：该\n                                                      机器当前聚焦的工作区。--raw 则会打印守护进程自身的\n                                                      LayoutDocument（精确的窗格/标签页 id）代替。\n  cmux vm layout apply <machine> (<file>|- | --from-saved <name>) [--workspace <workspace-id>|--name <name>] [--cwd <dir>] [--open]\n                                                      根据布局文档在机器上构建窗格、拆分和标签页：\n                                                      该文档可以是文件、标准输入（-）或保存在此 Mac 上的布局\n                                                      （`cmux layout list`）。默认值：一个以该文档命名的全新机器工作区\n                                                      （--name 可覆盖此名称）；--workspace 则用于指定一个\n                                                      已存在的空（EMPTY）工作区。终端的 `command` 会在\n                                                      在每个 surface 的 `cwd`（相对于\n                                                      --cwd，默认值：工作用户的家目录）中启动的登录 shell 内输入。--open 随后会在此处打开该工作区，\n                                                      并具有相同的几何布局。\n\n文档（以下之一）：\n  {\"pane\": {\"surfaces\": [{\"type\": \"terminal\", \"name\": \"tests\", \"command\": \"bun test\", \"cwd\": \"work/app\"}]}}\n  {\"direction\": \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\", \"split\": 0.6, \"children\": [<node>, <node>]}\n  {\"name\": …, \"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}      或      {\"name\": …, \"workspace\": {\"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}}\n`horizontal` = 并排（第一个子项在左），`vertical` = 堆叠（第一个子项在上）；`split` 是\n第一个子项的份额（0.1–0.9，默认值为 0.5）。Surface 类型：terminal (name, command, cwd, env)，\nbrowser (url, name)；project surface 仅限 Mac，在机器上会被跳过。\n工作区 id 来自 `cmux vm tree`。添加 --json 以获取原始结果。Exit 2 = 该文档无效。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "用法：\n  cmux vm layout export <machine> [<workspace-id|name>] [--raw]\n                                                      將機器工作區的版面配置列印為宣告式版面配置\n                                                      文件 — 也就是 `cmux new-workspace --layout`、\n                                                      `cmux layout save/open` 以及 cmux.json 所使用的同一個 JSON。預設值：\n                                                      機器目前聚焦的工作區。--raw 則會改為列印精靈程序本身的\n                                                      LayoutDocument（精確的窗格/索引標籤 ID）。\n  cmux vm layout apply <machine> (<file>|- | --from-saved <name>) [--workspace <workspace-id>|--name <name>] [--cwd <dir>] [--open]\n                                                      在機器上從版面配置\n                                                      文件建立窗格、分割和索引標籤：檔案、標準輸入 (-) 或儲存在此 Mac 上的版面配置\n                                                      （`cmux layout list`）。預設值：一個以該\n                                                      文件命名的全新機器工作區（可用 --name 覆寫）；--workspace 則是指定一個\n                                                      現有的空白工作區。終端機的 `command` 會被輸入到\n                                                      在每個介面的 `cwd` 中啟動的登入 shell 中（相對於\n                                                      --cwd，預設值：該工作使用者的家目錄）。接著 --open 會在此處開啟工作區，\n                                                      並具有相同的幾何尺寸。\n\n文件（其中之一）：\n  {\"pane\": {\"surfaces\": [{\"type\": \"terminal\", \"name\": \"tests\", \"command\": \"bun test\", \"cwd\": \"work/app\"}]}}\n  {\"direction\": \"horizontal\"|\"vertical\", \"split\": 0.6, \"children\": [<node>, <node>]}\n  {\"name\": …, \"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}      或      {\"name\": …, \"workspace\": {\"cwd\": …, \"layout\": <node>}}\n`horizontal` = 並排（第一個子項目在左側），`vertical` = 堆疊（第一個子項目在頂部）；`split` 是第一個\n子項目的佔比（0.1–0.9，預設為 0.5）。介面類型：terminal (name, command, cwd, env)、\nbrowser (url, name)；專案介面僅限 Mac，且在機器上會被跳過。\n工作區 ID 來自 `cmux vm tree`。加入 --json 來取得原始結果。Exit 2 = 文件無效。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
